description:
The .claude/settings.json file is using the old hook format. Hooks now require a 'matcher' object and 'hooks' array structure.

Current format:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "Stop": [
      {
        "type": "command",
        "command": ".claude/hooks/otto-stop-hook.sh"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

Required new format:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "Stop": [
      {
        "matcher": {},
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": ".claude/hooks/otto-stop-hook.sh"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

Add the prek tool (https://github.com/j178/prek) to the nix development shell.

**What is prek?**
prek is a pre-commit framework written in Go. It's faster than the Python-based pre-commit framework and is compatible with existing .pre-commit-config.yaml files.

**Why add prek?**
- Faster startup time than Python-based pre-commit
- Native Nix integration
- Can run nix build as a pre-commit hook
- Ensures code quality before commits

**Implementation approach:**

1. **Add prek to flake.nix inputs:**
   ```nix
   inputs = {
     nixpkgs.url = "github:NixOS/nixpkgs/nixos-unstable";
     flake-utils.url = "github:numtide/flake-utils";

     # Add prek
     prek = {
       url = "github:j178/prek";
       inputs.nixpkgs.follows = "nixpkgs";
     };
   };
   ```

2. **Add prek to devShell buildInputs:**
   ```nix
   devShells.default = pkgs.mkShell {
     buildInputs = with pkgs; [
       # ... existing inputs ...
       prek.packages..default
     ];
   };
   ```

**Alternative (simpler approach):**
If prek is available in nixpkgs:
```nix
devShells.default = pkgs.mkShell {
  buildInputs = with pkgs; [
    # ... existing inputs ...
    prek  # If available in nixpkgs
  ];
};
```

**Files to modify:**
- flake.nix (add prek input and buildInput)

**Verification:**
After adding, verify with:
```bash
nix develop
prek --version
prek --help
```

**Acceptance criteria:**
- prek is available in 'nix develop' shell
- 'prek --version' shows version
- 'prek --help' shows usage
- No errors when entering dev shell

**Next steps (not part of this issue):**
- Create .pre-commit-config.yaml with nix build hook
- Run 'prek install' to set up git hooks
- Configure hooks in flake.nix

**Note:**
This is just adding the tool to the dev shell. Configuring pre-commit hooks will be a separate issue (see otto-2u0).
